+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional date-only `dueDate`; the API filters overdue todos and the list page shows the date, an "überfällig" marker and a "nur überfällige" checkbox.
+
+**Architecture:** The store owns validation and the overdue rule (with an injectable `today` clock). `app.mjs` maps `?overdue=true` to the store filter. The page fetches `/todos` and `/todos?overdue=true` and never computes the rule itself.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, ES modules, `node:test`, no dependencies.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-due-date-design.md` (Ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` → HTTP 400.
+- TDD: failing test in `test/` first.
+- `dueDate` is `"YYYY-MM-DD"` or `null`; API always returns the field (`null` when unset).
+- Overdue = `done === false` and `dueDate` < today's UTC date (`new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`); no date → never overdue; due today → not overdue.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` filters; parameter absent → all todos; any other value → 400.
+- Page copy: date as `TT.MM.JJJJ`, marker text `überfällig`, checkbox label `nur überfällige`.
+- `data-testid`s: existing `todo-list`, `todo-item`, `todo-title` stay; new `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`, `overdue-filter`.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. A PATCH that changes only `title` or `done` must keep the existing `dueDate` → test in Task 1.
+2. A PATCH with a valid field plus an invalid `dueDate` (`{ title: 'X', dueDate: 'bad' }`) must return 400 and change nothing → test in Task 1 (validate all fields before mutating).
+3. Calendar edge cases: `2028-02-29` valid, `2027-02-29` and `2026-13-01` invalid; ISO timestamps like `2026-11-13T00:00:00Z` rejected → test in Task 1.
+4. A done todo with a past date that is PATCHed back to `done: false` shows up in the overdue filter again → test in Task 2.
+5. `?overdue=` (empty) and `?overdue=TRUE` are rejected with 400, not silently treated as "all" → test in Task 2.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: `dueDate` in the store and API
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs` (existing `creates and lists todos` expectation gains `dueDate: null`)
+- Create: `test/store.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `createStore({ today?: () => string } = {})`; todos shaped `{ id, title, done, dueDate: string | null }`; `add({ title, dueDate? })`; `update(id, { title?, done?, dueDate? })`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests** in `test/store.test.mjs` (direct store tests) and adjust `test/app.test.mjs`:
+  - `add without dueDate stores null` → `add({ title: 'A' }).dueDate === null`
+  - `add with dueDate stores it` → `add({ title: 'A', dueDate: '2026-11-20' }).dueDate === '2026-11-20'`
+  - `rejects invalid dueDates` → for each of `'2026-02-30'`, `'2027-02-29'`, `'2026-13-01'`, `'2026-11-13T00:00:00Z'`, `' 2026-11-20'`, `'morgen'`, `20261120`, `true`: `add` throws `ValidationError`
+  - `accepts leap day` → `add({ title: 'A', dueDate: '2028-02-29' })` succeeds
+  - `update changes and removes dueDate` → set `'2026-12-01'`, then `null` → `dueDate === null`
+  - `update without dueDate keeps it` → after `update(id, { title: 'B' })` and `update(id, { done: true })` the date is unchanged
+  - `invalid update changes nothing` → `update(id, { title: 'X', dueDate: 'bad' })` throws `ValidationError`; `get(id).title` still the old title
+  - app test: `creates and lists todos` expects `[{ id: 1, title: 'Milch kaufen', done: false, dueDate: null }]`; new `POST with invalid dueDate returns 400`
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `npm test` — Expected: the new tests FAIL.
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** in `src/store.mjs`: a private `validDueDate(value)` that accepts `null` or a string matching `/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/` whose `new Date(value + 'T00:00:00Z').toISOString().slice(0, 10) === value`; message `dueDate must be a date (YYYY-MM-DD) or null`. `update` validates every present field first, then mutates. `createStore` takes the `{ today }` option now (used in Task 2), default `() => new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run** `npm test` — Expected: all PASS.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** `git commit -am "feat: optional dueDate on todos (#1)"` (add `test/store.test.mjs` first).
+
+### Task 2: Overdue filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`, `src/app.mjs`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `createStore({ today })` from Task 1.
+- Produces: `store.list({ overdue?: boolean } = {})`; `GET /todos?overdue=true`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests** in `test/app.test.mjs`. Extend `withServer(fn, store = createStore())` to pass `createApp(store)`; use `createStore({ today: () => '2026-11-13' })`.
+  - `filters overdue todos`: create `past` (`2026-11-12`), `today` (`2026-11-13`), `future` (`2026-11-14`), `none` (no date), `donePast` (`2026-11-01`, then PATCH `done: true`) → `GET /todos?overdue=true` titles `['past']`; `GET /todos` returns all 5.
+  - `reopened todo is overdue again`: PATCH `donePast` to `done: false` → it appears in `?overdue=true`.
+  - `rejects other overdue values`: `?overdue=false`, `?overdue=`, `?overdue=TRUE`, `?overdue=1` → 400 each.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `npm test` — Expected: new tests FAIL.
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** `list({ overdue } = {})` in the store: when `overdue`, keep `!t.done && t.dueDate !== null && t.dueDate < today()` (string compare). In `app.mjs` GET `/todos`: `url.searchParams.has('overdue')` → value must be exactly `'true'`, else `throw new ValidationError('overdue must be "true"')`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run** `npm test` — Expected: all PASS.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** `git commit -am "feat: GET /todos?overdue=true filter (#1)"`.
+
+### Task 3: List page
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `public/index.html`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `GET /todos`, `GET /todos?overdue=true`, `dueDate` field.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test** `list page has overdue filter`: `GET /` body matches `/data-testid="overdue-filter"/` and `/nur überfällige/`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `npm test` — Expected: FAIL.
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** in `public/index.html`:
+  - Before the list: `<label><input type="checkbox" data-testid="overdue-filter"> nur überfällige</label>`.
+  - Load both endpoints in parallel. Build a set of overdue ids. Render with a `render(todos)` function: per item keep `todo-title` as it is, add `<span data-testid="todo-due-date">` with `TT.MM.JJJJ` built by splitting the string (no `new Date`) when `dueDate` is set, and `<span data-testid="todo-overdue">überfällig</span>` when the id is in the set.
+  - Checkbox `change` → `render(checked ? overdue : all)`. Separate spans with a space; use `textContent` only.
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run** `npm test` — Expected: all PASS.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** `git commit -am "feat: show due date and overdue filter on list page (#1)"`.
+
+End-to-end browser verification (agreed in the spec) runs after all tasks, before integration.
